# Recorded/synthetic test fixtures are byte-exact captures whose sha256 is
# asserted by tests/test_sample_coverage.py (content_hash). Any line-ending
# conversion would change the bytes and break that hash, so every fixture under
# tests/data is treated as binary: git must not normalize EOLs or strip trailing
# whitespace. This is what keeps the suite green on Windows, where
# actions/checkout enables core.autocrlf and would otherwise rewrite LF to CRLF.
tests/data/** -text
